tement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - 4y &= -4 \\\\\n-4y &= -4 + x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + x}{-4} \\\\\ny &= 1 - \\frac{1}{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,1 - \\frac{1}{4}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}] [{:db/id 17592186542476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ec9eaf-8a8c-5485-9397-f4080cccdb42" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{2}{7}x - \\frac{6}{7})" :db/id 17592186542459} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id 17592186542461} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab9055c-41fa-52d4-98cc-67b4d8dd46ac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3)" :db/id 17592186542484} {:answer/id #uuid "e29a0d02-5cca-5ff8-bf75-9db725841961" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x - 3)" :db/id 17592186542502} {:answer/id #uuid "f097021f-ff70-5357-a6ad-89cefc4a73f6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id 17592186542506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 